From 907a609b472666f1f57a9071a978d37a6c2092da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:44:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] WP29: No em dashes in user-visible copy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every em dash (U+2014) used as punctuation in a user-visible string is replaced
with a full stop, comma, colon or parentheses, with the meaning unchanged:

- i18n.py, in all five guest languages (en, cs, de, es, fr);
- host_i18n.py, including its interface strings;
- the legal catalogues (terms_i18n, privacy_policy_i18n, dpa_i18n), the public
  pages (landing_i18n) and the guest validation messages (validation_i18n);
- guide_i18n.py had none left;
- host templates that joined two pieces of text with a dash: guide.html
  (step title, colon), settings.html (retention and backup lines, comma; the
  missing-contact note now reads "...: A, B. Add one so ..."), and
  stay_fee_detail.html (period and adjustment reason in parentheses).

Placeholders: the select options "(none)" / "(select)" replace "— none —" and
"— select —"; a lone dash as an empty-cell placeholder stays. Legal and mail
templates had dashes only in Jinja comments, which are not rendered.

The legal texts change punctuation only, not meaning, so no legal version
moves.

New test tests/test_no_em_dashes.py fails if any string in any app/*_i18n.py
catalogue (or i18n.py) contains " — " or "— ", checks every guest language,
and checks the visible text of the legal and mail templates. Tests that pinned
the old wording are updated.
